error[int_out_of_range]: `3000000000` does not fit an `i32`
  at tests/golden/full/fixedbugs-2230-a-width-the-program-did-not-write-is-not-offered-to-widen.hero:30:20
     |
  30 |     print(twice(x: 3000000000))  #~ int_out_of_range
     |                    ^^^^^^^^^^
  note: an `i32` holds -2147483648 through 2147483647, and this one is the header's: `x` of `twice` is bound at the width its header gives it, as every parameter of an `extern` binding is (§4.19). Write a number in range — this language never truncates one silently

